# Why: the push credential in this environment is an OAuth App token without the `workflow`
# scope, so GitHub rejects any push that includes a commit touching .github/workflows/* — this
# hunk renames an AGENTS.md reference to CLAUDE.md, matching the repo-wide AGENTS.md -> CLAUDE.md
# rename (Claude Code auto-loads CLAUDE.md, not AGENTS.md, so the file was renamed and every
# reference updated).
#
# Apply from the repo root (e.g. `git apply docs/pending-changes/.github__workflows__test-matrix.yml.patch`),
# then delete this file, and commit + push both together yourself.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/test-matrix.yml b/.github/workflows/test-matrix.yml
index 4242bffd..375092b8 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/test-matrix.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/test-matrix.yml
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ jobs:
           go-version-file: go.mod
       - name: Run the auth/config permutation matrix
         # GitHub's own runners reach Docker Hub directly — --mirror is a sandbox-only workaround
-        # for the outbound proxy documented in AGENTS.md, so it is deliberately omitted here,
+        # for the outbound proxy documented in CLAUDE.md, so it is deliberately omitted here,
         # matching db-compat.yml's own comment for the identical reason. A scheduled run has no
         # workflow_dispatch inputs at all, so `inputs.kind` reads empty rather than its declared
         # default — treated the same as "all".
